{"seq":13,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T19:08:31.427Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"bc8f5596b01606ed2b772bd37443e25ff0f8616004a6e27561d1d9f98aba3b0f","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes. There are two:\n\n- #4419: Thea Ramaswell logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\", teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md\n- #PD-4492: Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at Eau Claire Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the kiosk. The SMS gateway was patched that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the 04:00 shift was fine. The note also says the Eau Claire kiosk logs were to be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025), teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md\n\nMoss's other two North notes mention Quarrendon but have no ticket numbers: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in. The tickets in Moss's Central notes (#4409, #4412, FR-882) are for other accounts, not QFL.\n\nOne more outside Moss's notes: your own 9 Apr 2026 renewal debrief with Thea mentions ticket #8841, a carrier portal timeout on CSV manifests over 600 rows."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
